-The findings can be stated at three levels. First, the literature suggests that AI is associated with organisational outcomes, mostly through complementary capabilities such as agility, innovation capability and organisational learning; in the strongest studies, the direct effect of AI disappears once these capabilities are considered. Second, the evidence partly supports the view that AI capability contributes to competitive advantage through such capabilities: four of the six hypotheses are partly supported, and none is fully supported. Third, the proposed mediation through sensing, seizing and transforming and the persistence of any advantage over time remain unconfirmed: mediation through seizing and transforming has not been examined, almost all studies are cross-sectional, the quality of most could not be assessed, and only seven concern e-commerce or platform-based business.
